      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so i am stuck on an iam policy issue. i have a lambda that needs to write logs to an s3 bucket but i keep getting access denied errors in the cloudwatch logs even though i think the policy is right. can you check this json for me?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\",\n        \"s3:GetBucketLocation\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The IAM policy you provided looks mostly correct, but it might be missing the necessary permissions for writing logs to CloudWatch. The policy doesn't explicitly allow writing to CloudWatch Logs. You'll need to add a statement that grants permission to ` logs:CreateLogGroup`, `logs:CreateLogStream`, and `logs:PutLogEvents`.\n\nHere's an updated policy that includes these permissions:\n\n```\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\",\n        \"s3:GetBucketLocation\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-app-logs-bucket/*\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"logs:CreateLogGroup\",\n        \"logs:CreateLogStream\",\n        \"logs:PutLogEvents\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:logs:*:*:*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
